OL,3,GNEWSATheatres at risk and fighting back
OL,4,Aacross the West
OL,5,
OL,6,FIn the space of a week, two theatres in
OL,7,Fthe West of England announced they
OL,8,Fwould be closing their doors.
OL,10,FTaunton Brewhouse said on 7 October
OL,11,Fthat it would shut at the end of the
OL,12,Fmonth, citing financial difficulties. A
OL,13,Fweek later, Bristol Improv Theatre
OL,14,Fannounced it would close with immediate
OL,15,Feffect due to its "very difficult and
OL,16,Fprecarious financial position".
OL,18,FOther theatres across the region are
OL,19,Fhaving to rely on government funding,
OL,20,Fcrowd funders and community takeover
OL,21,Fbids to keep their doors open.
OL,23,APub: 26-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
